okf_version: "1.0"
task: "sarah-ai (100.64.0.63:1004, Claude Code, Anthropic routed, ciel 0.2.51-nightly.20261005-063005.7a07765): Claude Code keeps answering 'Login expired · Please run /login' although one of the two stored Claude OAuth tokens is active."
reported: "User, 2026-10-05, screenshot: OAuth tokens panel '.credentials.json [limited · 7d 100%] claude-659e91' and 'kalvin... [active · 7d 46%] claude-1de5f7'; preflight 'Base URL: model list reachable, auth rejected (401)'."
access: "ssh -i ~/.ssh/aap_sarah-ai sarah-ai@100.64.0.63 -p 1004, read only. Token values never printed (lengths and timestamps only)."
confirmed:
  transcript: "~/.claude/projects/-home-sarah-ai/1d4ada0b-....jsonl: 53 assistant records isApiErrorMessage=true error=authentication_failed text 'Login expired · Please run /login', first 2026-10-04T11:02:20Z, latest 2026-10-05T06:47:13Z (150 ms after the user line)."
  claude_credentials: "~/.claude/.credentials.json mtime 2026-10-04T11:02:10Z: claudeAiOauth.accessToken length 0, refreshToken length 0, expiresAt 0 (refreshTokenExpiresAt kept). Claude Code's own credential is empty."
  ciel_store: "workspaces/d4e389cae4e1/oauth-tokens.state.json: claude-659e91 source 'import:/home/sarah-ai/.claude/.credentials.json', created 2026-10-04T06:01:13Z, refreshed_at 10:57:12Z (lock file oauth-refresh-claude-659e91.lock same time), 7d 100% (exhausted until reset), draining. claude-1de5f7 source 'login' (kalvin), active, 7d 46%, refreshed_at 13:52:13Z."
  router_side: "Session 1d4ada0b mapped to claude-1de5f7, seen_at 2026-10-04T11:02:11Z and not after; router.log at ERROR level has no auth lines. ciel code has no writer for ~/.claude/.credentials.json (only readers: oauth_token_endpoints, oauth_token_cli)."
timeline_utc: "06:01:13 ciel imports Claude Code's credential as claude-659e91 -> 10:57:12 ciel refreshes claude-659e91 -> 11:02:10 .credentials.json emptied -> 11:02:11 last routed request of the session -> 11:02:20 first 'Login expired'."
inferred_not_verified:
  - "ciel's refresh of the imported grant rotated the refresh token Claude Code also held; Claude Code's own refresh then failed and it cleared its credential. Who wrote the file at 11:02:10 is not proven (no Claude Code debug log)."
  - "With an empty local credential Claude Code stops before sending requests, so the active pool token never gets a chance (no router requests after 11:02:11)."
not_done: "Nothing changed on sarah; no code change."
fix:
  request: "User, 2026-10-05: '진행' (sync fix + restore sarah)."
  commit: "80c65fe fix(oauth): keep imported tokens in step with the CLI credential file. New ciel_runtime_support/oauth_import_sync.py; OAuthTokenRefresher.refresh adopts a credential the CLI refreshed first (file refresh token differs) inside the per-token lock, and after its own refresh writes access/refresh/expiry (Claude) or tokens + last_refresh (Codex) back into the import source, other fields kept, atomic replace keeping the file mode."
  tests: "unit 1727 OK (skipped 49; 6 new ImportedSourceSyncTests: write-back keeps other fields, CLI-refreshed credential adopted without a token request, rejected access token answered from the file, emptied file restored (sarah case), Codex auth.json in place, login-source tokens leave files alone); router 1175 OK; ruff and docs metadata clean; live router 9611 = 200."
  publish: "Pushed 7a07765..80c65fe; Actions run 37275691481 success; dist-tag nightly 0.2.51-nightly.20261005-070628.80c65fe."
  sarah: "npm install -g --prefix ~/.npm-global @one-ciel-ai/ciel-runtime@0.2.51-nightly.20261005-070628.80c65fe; VERSION matches. `ciel-runtime tokens refresh claude-659e91` -> 'refreshed; source updated' (rc 0). ~/.claude/.credentials.json: accessToken/refreshToken length 108 each, expiresAt 2026-10-05T15:17:28Z, subscriptionType max kept, mode 0600. `claude auth status` (2.1.289): loggedIn true, authMethod claude.ai, subscriptionType max."
  not_verified: "A Claude Code turn through ciel on sarah after the restore (sarah's terminal is at the ciel menu; not launched by me). The shared-grant race is narrowed, not removed: if Claude Code and the router refresh within the same moment, one side can still lose."
